# SRG-APP-000131-WSR-000051  -  CAT II
# All web server files must be verified for their integrity (e.g., checksums
# and hashes) before becoming part of the production web server.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000131-WSR-000051
group:           V-206372
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003992
control_rev5:    CM-14

contribution:    Splunk verifies on every startup, and on a recurring interval thereafter,
                 that the files installed with the running version still match the release
                 manifest, and reports any file that was removed or altered.

governs:         limits.conf - Limits on how much work searches and data processing may consume.

check:           limits.conf [system_checks] installed_files_integrity equals enabled
check:           limits.conf [system_checks] installed_files_integrity_interval non_empty

external:        Verification of installation media and app packages before they reach the
                 installation directory, carried by the operating system package manager's
                 signature checking and by the organization's software acceptance
                 procedure.
external:        app.conf [install] install_source_checksum records the checksum of the
                 package a given app was installed from, but the platform populates it
                 automatically and the specification directs that it not be set by hand, so
                 it is evidence rather than a control the assessor can require
                 (app.conf.spec:158).
external:        indexes.conf enableDataIntegrityControl hashes indexed data, not the
                 product's own installed files, so it does not bear on this objective
                 (indexes.conf.spec:594).

citation:        Web Server SRG SRG-APP-000131-WSR-000051 check text; limits.conf.spec:4450
                 (installed_files_integrity = enabled | log_only | disabled, default
                 enabled), limits.conf.spec:4468 (installed_files_integrity_interval,
                 default 12h), limits.conf.spec:4475
finding:         Splunk's installed-file integrity verification is not enabled, so the
                 application does not verify that the files of the running installation
                 still match the release manifest.
